From 2f201770cd4a3e3178c53c977aab172085f3d2d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Torokhov <dmitry.torokhov@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:11:01 -0700
Subject: Input: maplecontrol - emit EV_SYN report after reporting events
Git-commit: 2f201770cd4a3e3178c53c977aab172085f3d2d4
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc1
References: git-fixes

The driver decodes controller packets and reports button presses and
axis positions in dc_pad_callback(), but never calls input_sync() to
signal completion of the input report frame. Consequently, events
remain pending without waking up userspace readers.

Emit an EV_SYN/SYN_REPORT event after reporting buttons and axis states.

Fixes: 01461d7e65a6 ("Input: add support for Maple controller as a joystick")
Reported-by: sashiko-bot@kernel.org
Closes: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260704061045.036701F000E9@smtp.kernel.org
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dmitry Torokhov <dmitry.torokhov@gmail.com>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 drivers/input/joystick/maplecontrol.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/joystick/maplecontrol.c b/drivers/input/joystick/maplecontrol.c
index a498fc322c4d..1eb7d279965d 100644
--- a/drivers/input/joystick/maplecontrol.c
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/maplecontrol.c
@@ -58,6 +58,8 @@ static void dc_pad_callback(struct mapleq *mq)
 	input_report_abs(dev, ABS_Y,      res[13]);
 	input_report_abs(dev, ABS_RX,     res[14]);
 	input_report_abs(dev, ABS_RY,     res[15]);
+
+	input_sync(dev);
 }
 
 static int dc_pad_open(struct input_dev *dev)
